 important invariants","messageBody":"Several parser, command-dispatch, and task-model methods rely on\nassumptions established by their callers.\n\nBreaking these assumptions can cause failures far from their source, making\ndefects harder to diagnose.\n\nAdd assertions for valid command types, task indexes, task fields, and task\ncollections to help errors fail closer to their source.\n","tags":["A-FullCommitMessage"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":42,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"3a75e9cfb003c912c4a64d472466b612b4f34fb1","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Ui: Remove unused output methods","messageBody":"The console UI retains specialized output methods that no caller uses\nafter command responses move into Alex. Keeping them duplicates response\nformatting and obscures the active UI surface.\n\nRemove the dead methods and their now-unused imports so Ui contains only\nthe output paths used by the application.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":0,"deletions":85}}},{"hash":"cae814aa8cc69d78f72ade639b3d4bee4a8bf3db","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Alex: Consolidate task list formatting","messageBody":"List and find responses duplicate the same numbering and formatting\nloop. This makes a presentation change easy to apply inconsistently.\n\nCentralize the shared formatting in one helper while keeping each\ncommand responsible for selecting its heading and tasks.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":8,"deletions":15}}},{"hash":"291bb5879b72634801d9c5ab8414fac5169b1a07","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Alex: Clarify loading error name","messageBody":"The name loadingError does not reveal whether it stores an\nexception, a status, or display text, and the local name error is even\nless specific.\n\nRename both values to identify them as the message produced when task\nloading fails, making their role clear at each use site.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":8,"deletions":8}}},{"hash":"a15bea453e166a3e1c4c4253f4709a738c17fa81","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Parser: Name task date markers","messageBody":"The date markers are repeated as unexplained string literals when\nlocating and slicing command arguments. A marker change could leave\nparsing offsets or error messages inconsistent.\n\nIntroduce named constants for each marker and use them throughout\ndeadline and event parsing so their meaning and relationships are\nexplicit.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":18,"deletions":9}}},{"hash":"34b15d3b83061f7dbc1c2738b092c582721e6ae3","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Storage: Name serialized task fields","messageBody":"Task deserialization relies on numeric indexes, status flags, field\ncounts, and a split limit whose meanings are not evident at their use\nsites. These magic literals make the file format difficult to review.\n\nReplace them with grouped constants that describe each serialized field\nand format rule while preserving the existing on-disk representation.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":39,"deletions":16}}},{"hash":"cc46b40adb05c0ffac25ea93a97ef6a2b3b866e1","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Task: Simplify status icon expression","messageBody":"The trailing comment repeats the method Javadoc and the ternary\nexpression, while unnecessary parentheses add visual noise.\n\nKeep the expression self-explanatory and rely on the existing method\ncontract to document the returned status icons.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":1,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"ff72d612ad4edbd3b3ef02f1b5069933649d2a8e","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Storage: Separate task loading steps","messageBody":"loadTasks combines file access, iteration, deserialization, status\nrestoration, and error decoration in one long method. Mixing those\nabstraction levels obscures the normal loading path.\n\nExtract file reading and single-line parsing into focused methods so\nloadTasks presents only the high-level sequence while retaining\nline-specific errors.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":43,"deletions":22}}},{"hash":"efabac233c4d2012ae5baa63969d84f1bab7a180","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Tests: Remove redundant method comments","messageBody":"The test method names already state the behavior and expected outcome.\nTheir Javadocs repeat that information and add maintenance noise.\n\nRemove the redundant method comments while retaining class-level\ndocumentation that explains each test suite\u0027s scope.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":0,"deletions":70}}},{"hash":"32d0749fa02516ff0c4db91928c820a0caa0148a","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Main: Normalize import spacing","messageBody":"The package declaration and import block are separated by two blank\nlines, which breaks the file\u0027s otherwise consistent source layout.\n\nRemove the extra blank line so the import groups follow the project\u0027s\nstandard spacing.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":0,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"ae19a89440573678c2fb11d31068a2b2618f2ea4","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Use stream to parse command types","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":8,"deletions":15}}},{"hash":"8a014f72fe047aa9dcc3dcbd1ff4155c6742b0da","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #1 from jiangyuning07/branch-A-Assertions","messageBody":"Add assertions for important invariants","tags":["A-Assertions"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"82186d1758dad0b3323eefd91c917f8e046bdbd9","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027master\u0027 into branch-A-CodeQuality","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"5f3093c02af2ff411cdde2de05dc2c821d8c8c7b","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #2 from jiangyuning07/branch-A-CodeQuality","messageBody":"Improve code quality","tags":["A-CodeQuality"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"9ad1c7c0d71e914a25389bdec98ec09a97600415","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #3 from jiangyuning07/branch-A-Streams","messageBody":"Use stream to parse command types","tags":["A-Streams"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]},{"date":"2026-09-10T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"339126916fd2babe8186b8f1c0b2e9b067bbc0df","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Make task search case-insensitive","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":15,"deletions":4}}},{"hash":"cb9a6b85c89b4ba930c2d9792673de1af0366416","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #5 from jiangyuning07/branch-C-BetterSearch","messageBody":"Make task search case-insensitive","tags":["BCD-Extension"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]},{"date":"2026-09-15T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"b96269503553e22c9c96868501d5221064b03294","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Represent command outcomes explicitly","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":39,"deletions":8}}},{"hash":"681c67d04fb49e3ab55b7cf9f6a65d71d9daf68c","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Highlight command errors","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":17,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"20b5d2e1a4482f99cf09ceec6be90b6902ca8da0","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Make dialog widths responsive","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"fxml":{"insertions":1,"deletions":2},"java":{"insertions":4,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"a6f2408bfcdb8fbc1d9255dad2b30445539d5f59","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Differentiate user and Alex dialogs","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"fxml":{"insertions":3,"deletions":2},"java":{"insertions":7,"deletions":8}}},{"hash":"c1ed65f3f6f5d0797ea2d896aa1b09980acf6c6c","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Polish GUI interactions and styling","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"fxml":{"insertions":20,"deletions":18},"java":{"insertions":6,"deletions":0}}}]},{"date":"2026-09-16T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"42ff68fcfe1fc478f29c2d5bff74e3fd5ca9793d","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #7 from jiangyuning07/branch-A-BetterGUI","messageBody":"Improve GUI feedback","tags":["A-BetterGui"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"2cd8d214adc7159ecc37da917ef999b758dbf66a","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Support optional times for dated tasks","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":264,"deletions":27}}},{"hash":"2a52aa4a110609add353111b321f64b6a3ca22a7","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add upcoming deadline command","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":176,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"112154290147aa0d95fa636220546fee1b2c6f3a","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Report an error when find has no matches","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":12,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"360ac15bde92a624a9c995f7af6d36aaca00de7f","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #8 from jiangyuning07/branch-UpcomingDeadlines","messageBody":"Add upcoming deadline support","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"fbafab4edd89af9e2190f6d83dcc710f5c7740e7","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Preserve task state when saving fails","messageBody":"Task mutations remain in memory when persistence fails, so the displayed\nstate can differ from the data file and may be saved by a later command.\n\nRoll back add, delete, mark, and unmark operations when saving\nfails. Add a storage seam and regression tests that verify each command\npreserves the previous task state.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":134,"deletions":5}}},{"hash":"854e15abc1bf7d52bbb5eab00178369678c5d492","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Reject storage separators in descriptions","messageBody":"Task descriptions accept the pipe character even though storage uses it\nas a field separator. Saving such a description makes the data file\nunreadable on the next launch.\n\nReject pipe characters in todo, deadline, and event descriptions before\nconstructing the task. Add parser tests for all three task types.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":36,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"6ef9116b86e7d6845c4a53113aa40d543c171636","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Reject invalid event date ranges","messageBody":"Events accept end dates and times that are equal to or earlier than\ntheir starts, allowing invalid commands and malformed stored records.\n\nEnforce a strict end-after-start invariant in the Event model and\nconvert validation failures into user-facing command errors. Treat\nmissing times as the start of the date and cover command and storage\npaths with tests.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":77,"deletions":5}}},{"hash":"cb0ba8497678e998081e43cb5151f94860a42459","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Reject details on no-argument commands","messageBody":"Blank input is silently ignored in the GUI, while details after list,\nupcoming, or bye fall through to the generic unknown-command error.\n\nRecognize no-argument commands before validating their remaining text.\nReport specific errors for blank input and unexpected details so users\ncan correct malformed commands.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":88,"deletions":9}}},{"hash":"16f43b37eb7e4da0f1e188eacd4d09f30e035783","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Validate standalone schedule delimiters","messageBody":"Schedule parsing searches for marker substrings, so repeated or\nmisordered markers can produce unclear date errors or become task data.\nDelimiter-like description text can also be mistaken for syntax.\n\nRecognize only whitespace-bounded /by, /from, and /to tokens. Require\none /by for deadlines and one ordered /from and /to pair for events, and\nadd regression coverage for missing, repeated, misordered, and\ndelimiter-like cases.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":144,"deletions":13}}},{"hash":"43dada2342a6b3f6e725a7194ce4afa6bc184d0f","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #9 from jiangyuning07/branch-MoreErrorHandling","messageBody":"Improve error handling","tags":["A-MoreErrorHandling"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"db16a662a74631b86aae75034394ab707447f7ac","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Test core task management workflows","messageBody":"Command, parser, and storage behavior had gaps in successful persistence and malformed data handling.\n\n- Cover task creation and state changes across reloads.\n- Group required-field and storage validation cases to avoid repetition.\n- Verify event formatting and task-list snapshot immutability.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":256,"deletions":11}}},{"hash":"d957e7dbbf307aab2be08c06e038451bb56b819f","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #10 from jiangyuning07/branch-A-MoreTesting","messageBody":"Test core task management workflows","tags":["A-MoreTesting"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"a78ae7187d47b20a0d19429737e6b2899d5cf25a","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Give Alex a barista personality","messageBody":"Alex\u0027s neutral responses leave the chatbot without a distinctive voice.\n\nRewrite greetings, command acknowledgements, and validation errors with a\nmildly bored coffee-shop tone. Differentiate task-creation confirmations\nwhile preserving clear command guidance.\n\nUpdate response assertions so the new wording remains covered without\nchanging parsing, persistence, or task-state behavior.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":155,"deletions":118}}},{"hash":"9a34b93c421a9046b082958d0def1a35e2dbd314","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #11 from jiangyuning07/branch-A-Personality","messageBody":"Give Alex a barista personality","tags":["A-Personality"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"ea47fe04cbaf8cde1c67c1a2cdd98bafd67225bf","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Treat empty find results as normal output","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":4,"deletions":4}}}]}]},"authorFileTypeContributionMap":{"jiangyuning07":{"java":2694,"md":192,"fxml":89,"sh":0,"bat":0,"gradle":21,"txt":0}},"authorContributionVariance":{"jiangyuning07":102254.41},"authorDisplayNameMap":{"jiangyuning07":"CS2103T-T14-2 JIAN..NING"}}
